# Combined Configuration: Epistemic Weighting + Policy Averaging (EMA)
#
# Addresses both failure modes identified in Gen1 OU training:
#
# 1. Epistemic weighting (epistemic_aware_rl.gin):
#    - Problem: High Q-ensemble uncertainty → noisy advantages → directionally wrong gradients
#    - Solution: Weight actor gradients by inverse critic uncertainty: w = 1/(1 + β·σ̃)^p
#    - Target: Suppresses high-σ critic noise
#
# 2. Policy averaging (ema_config.gin):
#    - Problem: Strategic frequency drift in low-uncertainty regions (critic confident but wrong)
#    - Solution: Maintain EMA of policy params, evaluate EMA instead of current
#    - Target: Prevents accumulation of strategic drift (CFR-inspired)
#
# Why both mechanisms are needed:
#   - Epistemic weighting: Prevents bad gradients from uncertain regions ✅
#   - EMA: Prevents accumulation of small bad updates in confident regions ✅
#   - Expert analysis: "Epistemic weighting alone is insufficient - need equilibrium preservation"
#
# Expected behavior (combined):
#   - Epoch-0 win rate: ~40-50% (no catastrophic collapse)
#   - Stable learning: No cliff at epoch 1-2
#   - Frequency preservation: KL(ema || frozen) stays low
#   - Gradual improvement: Win rate increases smoothly over training
#
# ============================================================================
# Include Base Configurations
# ============================================================================

# Base config: aggressive reward scale + BC-heavy + dynamic damping
include 'metamon/rl/configs/training/selfplay_damped_aggressive.gin'

# Epistemic weighting: suppress high-σ gradients
include 'metamon/rl/configs/training/epistemic_aware_rl.gin'

# EMA: average policy for stability
include 'metamon/rl/configs/training/ema_config.gin'

# ============================================================================
# Combined Mechanism Behavior
# ============================================================================
# Both mechanisms run simultaneously and independently:
#
# During training step:
#   1. Compute actor/critic losses (per-timestep)
#   2. Apply epistemic weighting: actor_loss *= confidence(σ)  [BEFORE masked_avg]
#   3. Compute scalar loss via masked_avg
#   4. Add KL damping loss (if enabled)
#   5. Backward pass + optimizer step
#   6. Update EMA weights: ema = decay * ema + (1-decay) * current
#
# During evaluation:
#   1. Swap to EMA weights
#   2. Run evaluation battles
#   3. Restore training weights
#
# During checkpointing:
#   - Save regular checkpoint: {ckpt_dir}/policy_weights/policy_epoch_{N}.pt
#   - Save EMA checkpoint: {ckpt_dir}/ema_weights/policy_epoch_{N}.pt
#
# ============================================================================
# Key Configuration Summary
# ============================================================================
# From selfplay_damped_aggressive.gin:
#   - reward_multiplier = 0.05 (for +200/0 reward scale)
#   - offline_coeff = 0.75, online_coeff = 0.25 (BC-heavy)
#   - target_kl_per_step = 0.015 (loose KL target)
#   - kl_coef_init = 0.30 (strong initial damping)
#
# From epistemic_aware_rl.gin:
#   - use_epistemic_weighting = True
#   - epistemic_beta_init = 5.0 → epistemic_beta_final = 1.0
#   - epistemic_power = 2 (quadratic tail suppression)
#   - epistemic_anneal_steps = 10000 (~3 epochs)
#
# From ema_config.gin:
#   - use_ema = True
#   - ema_decay = 0.999 (~1000 step window)
#   - ema_update_interval = 1 (every gradient step)
#   - ema_eval_only = True (eval uses EMA, training uses current)
#
# ============================================================================
# Metrics to Monitor
# ============================================================================
# Epistemic weighting metrics:
#   - Epistemic/Mean Confidence: Should start ~0.5-0.7, increase over training
#   - Epistemic/Confidence (High σ): ~0.3-0.5
#   - Epistemic/Confidence (Low σ): ~0.7-0.9
#   - Epistemic/Effective Mass: > 0.5 (learning not suppressed)
#   - Epistemic/Beta: Decays from 5.0 → 1.0
#
# EMA metrics:
#   - EMA initialization message at training start
#   - EMA weight swap messages during evaluation
#   - EMA checkpoints in {ckpt_dir}/ema_weights/
#
# Training health:
#   - KL divergence: < 0.02 (not exploding)
#   - Entropy: > 1.0 (no collapse)
#   - Win rate: Should NOT drop to 0% at epoch 0-1
#
# ============================================================================
# Success Criteria
# ============================================================================
# Primary metric: Epoch-0 win rate vs RandomBaseline
#   ❌ Failure: < 30% (catastrophic collapse)
#   ⚠️ Partial: 30-40% (some collapse)
#   ✅ Success: > 40% (maintains baseline performance)
#
# Secondary metrics:
#   - No catastrophic cliff at epoch 1-2 (gradual learning curve)
#   - EMA policy outperforms current policy by epoch 2+
#   - Policy entropy stable (H > 1.0 throughout)
#   - KL divergence stable (< 0.02 throughout)
#
# ============================================================================
# Troubleshooting
# ============================================================================
# If still seeing epoch-0 collapse (< 40% win rate):
#   1. Check epistemic weighting is active (Effective Mass logged)
#   2. Increase epistemic_beta_init (5.0 → 8.0 or 10.0)
#   3. Increase epistemic_power (2 → 3 for stronger suppression)
#   4. Verify EMA is enabled (EMA initialization logged)
#
# If learning is too slow (epoch 2-3 no improvement):
#   1. Check Effective Mass > 0.5 (if < 0.5, epistemic too aggressive)
#   2. Lower epistemic_beta_init (5.0 → 3.0)
#   3. Lower epistemic_power (2 → 1 for gentler weighting)
#   4. Increase ema_decay slightly (0.999 → 0.9995)
#
# If EMA policy is too volatile:
#   1. Increase ema_decay (0.999 → 0.9999)
#   2. Consider adding KL-to-frozen constraint (future work)
#
# If EMA policy is too conservative:
#   1. Decrease ema_decay (0.999 → 0.99)
#   2. Try ema_eval_only = False (use EMA for training too)
#
# ============================================================================
# Usage
# ============================================================================
# Standard Gen1 OU training with combined mechanisms:
#   python -m metamon.rl.finetune_from_hf \
#       --run_name "epistemic_ema_gen1ou" \
#       --finetune_from_model DampedBinarySuperV1_Epoch4 \
#       --custom_replay_dir ~/metamon/trajectories/super_dataset_loop3/ \
#       --formats gen1ou \
#       --train_gin_config epistemic_ema_rl.gin \
#       --reward_function AggressiveShapedRewardSleep \
#       --obs_space ExpandedObservationSpace \
#       --epochs 3 \
#       --save_dir ~/metamon/models/epistemic_ema_test \
#       --eval_gens 1 \
#       --log
#
# Evaluate EMA checkpoint vs current checkpoint:
#   # Current policy (epoch 2)
#   python -m metamon.rl.evaluate \
#       --model_name YourModel \
#       --checkpoint_path ~/metamon/models/epistemic_ema_test/ckpts/policy_weights/policy_epoch_2.pt
#
#   # EMA policy (epoch 2)
#   python -m metamon.rl.evaluate \
#       --model_name YourModel \
#       --checkpoint_path ~/metamon/models/epistemic_ema_test/ckpts/ema_weights/policy_epoch_2.pt
#
# ============================================================================
# Next Steps (If Combined Approach Still Insufficient)
# ============================================================================
# If epoch-0 collapse persists despite both mechanisms:
#   1. Add KL-to-frozen policy constraint (next intervention from expert)
#   2. Add actor update ramp: α(t) = 0 → 1 over first epoch
#   3. Consider frequency-aware FBC filtering
#   4. Consider policy mixing: π = (1-α)*π_frozen + α*π_learned
#
# Expert recommended priority:
#   1. KL-to-frozen constraint (most important)
#   2. Actor update ramp (simpler to implement)
#   3. Frequency-aware filtering (more advanced)
